#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Design a game UI theme as tokens, look at it, then hand the same tokens to the Roblox kit.

  uitheme sheet [themes.json] [--only Name] [--out dir]   render a phone-size preview of every theme (PNG)
  uitheme luau  [themes.json] [--out Themes.luau]         write the token tables the Luau UiKit reads
  uitheme new   <Name> --from <Existing> [themes.json]    copy a theme to start a bespoke one

A theme is ONLY tokens (colour roles, shape, type, motion). Components never name a colour; they ask for
a role ("primary", "surface", "outline"). So a bespoke kit for a new game is: copy the nearest theme,
change tokens, render the sheet, look at it at phone size, repeat. The sheet shows the three states a
theme has to survive: HUD over a bright world, a shop panel with rarity cards, a result modal with one
primary action. Preview is HTML drawn with the same geometry as the kit (lip, stroke, radius, 844x390
reference); fonts are the Google versions of Roblox's built-in families. Needs a Chromium (Playwright's
cache or Google Chrome) and network for fonts/icons on first render.
"""
